===============================================================================
ADVISORY FINDINGS
===============================================================================

A1 (advise) — THE ROUND-1 CERTIFICATES WERE OVERWRITTEN IN PLACE, NOT LEFT AS
RESIDUE. f0071a4 does not merely add the 0eacc4a0 trio; it rewrites all three
round-1-era files:

  studio/ci/W-035-lint-6ecf88f1.log   -certifies: tree:6ecf88f1…  +certifies: dirty:6ecf88f1…
  studio/ci/W-035-types-6ecf88f1.log  -certifies: tree:6ecf88f1…  +certifies: dirty:6ecf88f1…
  studio/ci/W-035-tests-6ecf88f1.log  -certifies: tree:6ecf88f1…  +certifies: dirty:6ecf88f1…

Three files, one class, and I checked there is no fourth: those are the only
studio/ci paths modified (as opposed to added) in ddc42ca..f0071a4, per
`git log --name-status`. The tests log's body also moved (per-request timings
1ms→2ms), so this was a genuine re-run, not a hand edit.

Root cause, and it is not W-035's code: packages/pipeline/src/index.ts:99
names the log `${opus.id}-${probatioId}-${tree8}.log` from the source hash
alone, while line 70 puts the dirty/clean distinction only in the body's
`certifies:` line. A `--allow-dirty` run at the same HEAD therefore silently
clobbers the clean certificate for that same source tree. The builder's dirty
round-2 run at HEAD=ddc42ca (source 6ecf88f1) landed on top of the clean
round-1 certificates for 6ecf88f1.

Not blocking: the three clobbered files are unreferenced (nothing in studio/
names them — I grepped), opera/W-035.md points only at the honest 0eacc4a0
trio, and studio/ci/W-035-review-1.log itself is untouched. But my round-1
verdict's header cites those three as `tree:`, and on the branch they no
longer read that way. The mechanism is pre-existing and has bitten before
(same in-place flip visible in the W-037 and ci-round-2 commits), so it is a
tool gap for the retro, not a W-035 defect: a certificate filename should
carry the dirty/clean distinction, or a dirty run should refuse to overwrite
a clean certificate at the same hash.

A2 (advise) — REBASE WILL STALE THE CERTIFICATES. Master has moved to 786fa2a
(.github/workflows/ci.yml permissions). `.github/` is inside the source tree
hash, so rebasing opus/W-035 onto master moves the source hash off
0eacc4a0 and `probatio.certifies.stale` will fire on all three gates.
It is advisory only (check.ts:464), so `check` will not fail — but the gates
must be re-run after the rebase before the merge gate is meaningful. This is
the orchestrator's landing step, flagged here only so it is not forgotten.

Round-1 advisories A1-A5 and brief defects BD1-BD3 stand unchanged and were
not in round 2's scope. Round-1 A1 in particular still holds: 18.log records
`# command: node --import tsx packages/cli/src/retro.test.ts .` and carries
behaviours 10-18, because retro.test.ts still has no `--only` selector.
`opus.red_content` does not fire.

